<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-24",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-24",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "treadmill with netflix",
      "best treadmill with netflix",
      "treadmill netflix",
      "treadmill that streams netflix",
      "treadmill with youtube",
      "treadmill with disney plus",
      "treadmill touchscreen streaming",
      "treadmill with tv screen",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best Overall: Bowflex T16", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/best/">Best Treadmills</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buying Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Best Treadmills With Netflix Which Screens Actually Stream</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        The best treadmill for watching Netflix is the Bowflex T16: its Amazon listing says the 16-inch console streams Netflix, Prime Video and Spotify, and Bowflex says the treadmill works without a JRNY membership. Aviron’s Victory names the longest app list, including Disney+ and YouTube, and NordicTrack’s T Series 10 is the cheapest established-brand option, as long as you pay for iFIT Pro.
      </p>
      <p class="ed-answer"><strong>Short answer.</strong> Best Overall: <a href="#bowflex-t16">Bowflex T16</a>. Widest App List: <a href="#aviron-victory">Aviron Victory Treadmill</a>. Best for iFIT Members: <a href="#nordictrack-t-series-10">NordicTrack T Series 10</a>.</p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 24, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">How we chose: makers’ published specifications and manuals, independent reviews and owner reports, cross-checked. Not tested hands-on.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We may earn a commission when you buy through the links below. It costs you nothing and never decides a ranking. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#bowflex-t16"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31I8-29nvEL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Bowflex T16" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#aviron-victory"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31e36FphrXL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Aviron Victory Treadmill" width="500" height="476" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#nordictrack-t-series-10"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31zk9ulTbQL._SL500_.jpg" alt="NordicTrack T Series 10" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Bowflex T16 · Aviron Victory Treadmill · NordicTrack T Series 10</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          A big touchscreen on a treadmill looks as if it should play anything a tablet can. Most of
          them do not. Some consoles run only the maker’s own workout software, some add a short list
          of approved streaming apps behind the top membership tier, and a few run an open app store
          and a web browser. Amazon listings rarely make the difference clear, because “streaming” in
          a title can mean anything from Netflix to trainer-led classes. This page sorts the treadmills
          on Amazon that say, in their listing or on their maker’s site, which streaming apps they run,
          what each one needs before Netflix will open, and when a $30 tablet holder is the better buy.
          We only name an app as supported where the listing or the maker names it.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Overall:</span> <a href="#bowflex-t16">Bowflex T16</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Widest App List:</span> <a href="#aviron-victory">Aviron Victory Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best for iFIT Members:</span> <a href="#nordictrack-t-series-10">NordicTrack T Series 10</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
