        <div id="how-we-chose" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>How We Chose These Treadmills</h2>
<p>
            Not tested hands-on; picked from listings, specs and owner reviews. We did not run on these
            machines or sign in to their apps. We searched Amazon US for treadmill listings that mention
            streaming, Netflix or a TV screen, read each candidate’s listing through Amazon’s product API
            on 24 November 2026, and compared it with what the maker states and with this site’s existing
            reviews of the same machines.
          </p>
          <p>
            A treadmill had to clear four bars. <strong>Its listing or maker had to say the console
            streams entertainment</strong>, not only workout video. <strong>It had to be in stock on Amazon
            US with a price showing</strong> on the day we checked. <strong>It had to come from a named
            brand</strong> with a storefront or support contact beyond one listing. And <strong>it had to
            give a different answer to the Netflix question</strong> from the others, so the page covers
            the main ways a treadmill screen can handle streaming: open, approved-list, membership-gated
            and unnamed.
          </p>
          <p>
            We gave most weight to what the source actually names. A listing that names Netflix scores
            above one that says “stream your favourite shows”, because the second could mean a browser,
            a short app list or a workout channel. We gave little weight to screen size on its own, and
            none to star ratings. Treadmill specifications (deck, motor, weight limit, warranty) are
            on each card because a screen is useless on a treadmill you do not want to run on.
          </p>
          <p>
            This page differs from our <a href="/best-treadmills-with-screens/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best treadmills with screens</a> guide, which ranks touchscreen treadmills on the machine and the class platform. Here the
            only question is what the screen will play.
          </p>
        </div>

